 61NI c  No changes made since the 2015 update                                  
 61NI c  1996Ma11: (pol p,d): E(p)=65 MeV, FWHM|?40 keV. Measured |s(E(d),|q),  
 61NI2c  and analyzing powers, DWBA analysis.                                   
 61NI c  2013Sc06, 2013ScZZ: (p,d), E(p)=28 MeV from WNSL-Yale tandem           
 61NI2c  accelerator facility. Measured deuteron spectra, |s(|q), spectroscopic 
 61NI3c  factors C{+2}S using a split-pole Enge spectrograph. FWHM |?48 keV.    
 61NI4c  Target=219 |mg/cm{+2} thick 96.5% enriched. Deduced levels, J, |p.     
 61NI5c  DWBA analysis. Comparison with shell-model calculations.               
 61NI c  The main purpose of the neutron adding and neutron removal reaction    
 61NI2c  studies by 2013Sc06 was to obtain occupancies of neutron orbitals,     
 61NI3c  proton vacancies, and energy centroids of neutron, neutron-holes,      
 61NI4c  proton-single particle excitations in {+60}Ni and {+62}Ni, and thereby 
 61NI5c  investigate closure of 0f{-7/2} shell. Some data details of this study 
 61NI6c  are supplied in 2013ScZZ                                               
 61NI c  1976Ko06: (p,d): E(p)=40 MeV. Measured |s(E(d),|q), 14 angles between  
 61NI2c  4|' and 54|', magnetic spectrograph, FWHM|?45 keV, enriched target.    
 61NI c  Others: 1979Ik04, 1974Ko32, 1965Sh06 (12 levels up to 9550 keV).       
 61NI c  All data are from 1996Ma11, except as noted.                           
